  "term": "Bone Conduction",
  "definition": "Bone conduction is the transmission of sound to the inner ear through vibrations of the skull bones rather than through the ear canal and eardrum. It can be used to estimate cochlear hearing levels while bypassing problems in the outer or middle ear.",
